# TEMPLATE for `tests/evals/model_fixtures.yaml` (gitignored).
# Copy to model_fixtures.yaml and point each fixture at a real video from
# YOUR corpus. The real file stays private: which videos a maintainer indexes,
# annotated with the defect each one exposes, is a curated watchlist extract -
# more revealing than the bare URLs. Same split as config.yaml / config.yaml.example.
#
# Fixture set for `python scripts/model_eval.py` - the model A/B matrix.
#
# Each fixture names ONE facet the pipeline can fail on. The point is coverage of
# failure modes, not statistical power: a model that looks great on a clean
# talking-head monologue can still collapse a screen-share demo into one
# undifferentiated block, and only a fixture that PROBES that will show it.
#
# Segments are short (default 10 min) and deliberately not from the start of the
# video where an intro can flatter a model. Everything is read-only: the harness
# calls Gemini against the YouTube URL and writes only into its own scratch dir.
#
# Adding a fixture is cheap and encouraged. Removing one needs a reason - each is
# here because it represents a way the transcript step has actually degraded.

defaults:
  segment_seconds: 600
  media_resolution: low

fixtures:
  - id: screenshare-demo
    facet: >-
      Screen-share with live terminal/editor output. Probes on-screen text capture
      and the monolithic-collapse failure: the shape where a model transcribes the
      words correctly but stamps minutes of content as one block, destroying the
      &t= deep-link precision the corpus exists for.
    url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=REPLACE_ME
    channel: your_channel
    start: 0

  - id: multi-speaker-podcast
    facet: >-
      Two-plus speakers with interruption and crosstalk. Probes diarization: whether
      distinct voices are separated or merged into one speaker.
    url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=REPLACE_ME
    channel: your_channel
    start: 1200

  - id: talking-head-monologue
    facet: >-
      Single presenter, minimal visual aid, dense continuous speech. The easy case -
      a model that degrades HERE is disqualified outright.
    url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=REPLACE_ME
    channel: your_channel
    start: 900

  - id: long-form-midpoint
    facet: >-
      Deep inside a 90-min+ video, away from any intro. Probes whether quality holds
      at a chunk boundary rather than only in the opening minutes.
    url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=REPLACE_ME
    channel: your_channel
    start: 3000
